    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d859">

                <pb facs="1160" n="1040" xml:id="pg1040"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">837.51/833: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Representative on Special Mission in Cuba</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Crowder</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Acting
                        Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Habana</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1922-09-07T19:00:00-05:29"><hi rendition="#italic">September 7,
                                1922—7 p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received 10:13
                    p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>59. Referring to your 61, September 6, paragraph three. Mr. Meyer,<anchor n="48"
                        xml:id="d859-f1"/> after personal conference with Secretary Despaigne,
                    reports this evening that the revenues for the months of July and August
                    exceeded the budget obligations for those months by $527,000.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Crowder</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d859-f1" n="48" xml:id="d859-f1-content">
                <p>Secretary of American Legation at Habana.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
